## Exam-Style Questions — Test Your Understanding

**Q1: What role is required to invite guest users without full User Administrator privileges?**
> The **Guest Inviter** role allows a user to send B2B invitations to external users
> without granting any other administrative capabilities. This follows the principle
> of least privilege.

**Q2: A user's email address is `jane+work@partner.com`. What should you enter in the invite form?**
> Enter `jane@partner.com` — omit the plus symbol and everything between
> the + and the @ symbol. Microsoft Entra ID does not support plus symbols
> in email addresses and it will cause delivery failures.

**Q3: What does the User type column show for an external guest in the All Users list?**
> The User type column shows **Guest** for external B2B users, compared to
> **Member** for internal users created in your tenant.

**Q4: What are the two required columns in the bulk invite CSV template?**
> 1. `Email address to invite` — the guest's email address
> 2. `Redirection url` — where the guest is sent after accepting the invitation

**Q5: What is the difference between B2B collaboration and B2C?**
> **B2B** is for partner/vendor/contractor collaboration — external users
> use their own organisational identity to access your resources as guests.
> **B2C** is for customer-facing scenarios — consumers create their own accounts
> to access your public-facing applications. They are separate products and
> use separate tenants.

**Q6: A guest user accepted the invitation but cannot access a shared app. What is the most likely cause?**
> The guest has not been assigned access to the specific application.
> Accepting an invitation only creates the guest account in the directory —
> it does not automatically grant access to any resources. The admin must
> assign the guest to the required app, group, or resource separately.

**Q7: Can you invite a guest using a shared mailbox or distribution group email?**
> No. Group email addresses are not supported for B2B invitations.
> You must use an individual user's email address only.

